  "notes": "A tongue-in-cheek 'Palantir for family trips': ops-center vocabulary (UNCLASSIFIED // FAMILY OPS, mission scrub, response plans, travel units, call sign, weather intel NOAA) applied to a group vacation. GitHub-dark palette with semantic hue per family/lane (amber, red, purple, blue, green). Near-square 1-2px radii, 1px #30363d hairline borders, tracked uppercase micro-labels with blue eyebrow headings. Floating translucent panels over the map. Timeline has playback controls (play, restart, 1x speed) for replaying trip state over time, plus a daily weather row above swimlanes and a 'now' marker. Selection in any view (travel unit, timeline bar, time scrub) propagates to map, situation lists and the right detail aside."
